{
  "case_id": "2020-19-309",
  "document_hash": "a3650e846e2e5cab857e329095e3eb6a017d5ab0a6ded7637d28791e0e1ee46d",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-19-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a3650e846e2e5cab857e329095e3eb6a017d5ab0a6ded7637d28791e0e1ee46d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a3650e846e2e-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Our first case today is Number 19-309, John Carney, Governor of Delaware, versus James Adams. Mr. McConnell."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2020-19-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a3650e846e2e5cab857e329095e3eb6a017d5ab0a6ded7637d28791e0e1ee46d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a3650e846e2e-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Delaware constitution pass muster under the First Amendment. And Mr. Adams, who passed up the chance to apply for a host of judgeships both before and after changing party affiliation, lacks standing to challenge either one."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2020-19-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a3650e846e2e5cab857e329095e3eb6a017d5ab0a6ded7637d28791e0e1ee46d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a3650e846e2e-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Thomas: Thank you, Chief Justice. Mr. McConnell, I'd like to just move to the merits briefly. How -- I'd like to know how far you'd go with your argument. Could Delaware, for example, pass a law requiring all judges to be members of one or the other of the major parties?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2020-19-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a3650e846e2e5cab857e329095e3eb6a017d5ab0a6ded7637d28791e0e1ee46d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a3650e846e2e-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Thomas: Well, what -- what, for -- would this be -- would your case be better or worse if this were not a matter of constitutional provision but, rather, a matter of a tradition or practice that had a long standing?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2020-19-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a3650e846e2e5cab857e329095e3eb6a017d5ab0a6ded7637d28791e0e1ee46d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a3650e846e2e-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Alito: Mr. McConnell, what do you think is the minimum that Mr. Adams would have to allege in order to have standing? Suppose he looked up when the next vacancy would occur on any of the covered courts and said, I plan to apply for that position. Would that be sufficient?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2020-19-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a3650e846e2e5cab857e329095e3eb6a017d5ab0a6ded7637d28791e0e1ee46d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a3650e846e2e-0000-0012",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "He's -- that certainly fall shorts of a concrete plan, as required by Lujan, but I think his big problem is that --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2020-19-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a3650e846e2e5cab857e329095e3eb6a017d5ab0a6ded7637d28791e0e1ee46d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a3650e846e2e-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How -- how about with respect to the major party requirement? What analogues do you have for that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2020-19-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a3650e846e2e5cab857e329095e3eb6a017d5ab0a6ded7637d28791e0e1ee46d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a3650e846e2e-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, although I can't point to a specific use of this particular matter, this Court has approved any number of limitations on First Amendment rights as a condition to public service. The Hatch Act cases, for example, are a much more severe limitation on free speech rights, applying to lots more people for lots more positions, and the Court has --has consistently upheld them."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAVANAUGH",
      "case_id": "2020-19-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a3650e846e2e5cab857e329095e3eb6a017d5ab0a6ded7637d28791e0e1ee46d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a3650e846e2e-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "On the merits question, could a state exclude Republicans and Democrats from being judges and allow only Independents to be judges?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2020-19-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a3650e846e2e5cab857e329095e3eb6a017d5ab0a6ded7637d28791e0e1ee46d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a3650e846e2e-0001-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If this Court accepts the premise, it's the end of the idea of an independent judiciary."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
      "case_id": "2020-19-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a3650e846e2e5cab857e329095e3eb6a017d5ab0a6ded7637d28791e0e1ee46d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a3650e846e2e-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And if we view that in the light most favorable to the other side, can we say that means that he would actually apply?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2020-19-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a3650e846e2e5cab857e329095e3eb6a017d5ab0a6ded7637d28791e0e1ee46d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a3650e846e2e-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, had you withdrawn the -- the -- the request for an injunction?\nMR. FINGER: We've taken no action on the injunction issue."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2020-19-309",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a3650e846e2e5cab857e329095e3eb6a017d5ab0a6ded7637d28791e0e1ee46d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a3650e846e2e-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Counsel, your last answer troubles me because there are three rights at issue here that I see, at least three."
    },
